DOI 10.1214/aos/1176349846
title: Gaussian Markov Distributions over Finite Graphs
authors: Speed, Kiiveri
issued: 1986-03-01
container: The Annals of Statistics
volume: 14
page: 138-150
type: journal-article
abstract: Gaussian Markov distributions are characterised by zeros in the inverse of their covariance matrix and we describe the conditional independencies which follow from a given pattern of zeros.

DOI 10.1111/j.2517-6161.1974.tb00999.x
title: Spatial Interaction and the Statistical Analysis of Lattice Systems
authors: Besag
issued: 1974-01-01
container: Journal of the Royal Statistical Society Series B: Statistical Methodology
volume: 36
page: 192-225
type: journal-article
abstract: A simple alternative proof of the Hammersley–Clifford theorem is presented and the theorem is then used to construct specific spatial schemes on and off the lattice. Particular emphasis is placed upon practical applications of the models in plant ecology when the variates are binary or Gaussian.

