DOI 10.1093/oso/9780198522195.001.0001
title: Graphical Models
authors: Lauritzen
issued: 1996-05-02
type: book
abstract: The idea of modelling systems using graph theory has its origin in several scientific areas: in statistical physics (the study of large particle systems), in genetics (studying inheritable properties of natural species), and in interactions in contingency tables. The use of graphical models in statistics has increased considerably over recent years and the theory has been greatly developed and extended. This book provides the first comprehensive account of the theory of graphical models.

